note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note seed/ng/src/opt.om: the ΩIR optimizer of the ng compiler (Hive NG D16, M3). Owner: ng-ir lane. A unit of
note seed/ng/ng.units after ir.om; no fn main. Functions op_*, globals o_*. It rewrites the ir.om tables in place
note between ir_read and ir_wr (main's modes `@ng opt` and `@ng opt-count`): it moves ops between blocks and
note blocks within a function, adds blocks and drops ops, through the same lists ir_wr walks.
note Per function, in order:
note 1. Preheaders. Every natural loop (header h, a back edge u -> h with h dominating u, the loop being the blocks
note    that reach a latch without passing h) gets one block outside it that is h's only predecessor from outside:
note    the existing one when h has exactly one outside predecessor and it ends in `br h`; otherwise a new block,
note    placed before h, with h's parameter types, ending in `br h` with them, which every outside predecessor
note    branches to instead (same arguments).
note 2. BCE (IR.md s15 item 1, origin 1 of the pass table below). A `chk.bounds r i e` is deleted when e is a
note    const >= 1, r a REF to an ARRAY of count L, and i < X is known where the check runs, with X - 1 + e <= L:
note    i is a const (X = i + 1), or a block on the check's dominator path has one predecessor, which ends in
note    a `cbr` on `lt`/`le`/`gt`/`ge` of i and a const (either edge, read accordingly), so that block runs
note    only after the test said i < X. The check is replaced in place by `fact.inbounds 1 r i e`, which keeps
note    every access covered (s8). A `chk.divz` of a nonzero const is deleted. Uses of a deleted check's
note    output token take its input token, so the chain stays linear (s6.4).
note 3. LICM, innermost loop first. An op of the loop (blocks in reverse postorder, ops in order) moves to the end
note    of the preheader, before its `br`, when its class is P (IR.md s6.4: no token; every P op is total, s7.3, so
note    it may run on a path where it did not), it defines a value, it is not `shared` (block 0 only), and every
note    operand is defined outside the loop. Checks, loads, stores, calls, host words, facts and terminators never
note    move: the token chain and coverage (s6.4, s8, s15) fix their places. An op equal to one already in the
note    preheader (op, type, imm and operands) is dropped and its uses take the earlier value.
note 4. ROT. A loop whose header ends in `cbr` with one target in the loop and one outside, and whose one latch
note    ends in `br h`, gets its header placed right after that latch. The block order is the layout a back end
note    emits (a64 falls through to the next block and branches on one side of a `cbr`), so the back branch falls
note    through into the test and the loop is tested at the bottom: one conditional branch per pass. Block order
note    changes no value: uses are judged by dominance (s6.2).
note Pass table (fact origins, IR.md s7.10): 1 BCE.
note `@ng opt-count` runs the same passes and prints one line instead of the unit:
note "opt fns=F loops=L inloop=A->B bce=C hoisted=H merged=M rotated=R preheaders=P": L natural loops (by header),
note A and B the executing ops in loop blocks before and after (static, terminators included, facts not; a block
note counts once however
note deeply it nests), C checks deleted by BCE, H moves of an op out of a loop (an op leaving two nested loops counts twice; M of them
note dropped as equal to one already in the preheader), R headers placed after their latch, P preheader blocks
note added.
note
note per block handle: o_bp position in its function, o_bl block at position, o_rn reverse postorder number (from
note 1; 0 not reached), o_ro block at rpo number, o_id immediate dominator, o_pc predecessor count, o_p0 first
note predecessor in o_pl, o_lm loop mark (a stamp), o_sk next successor in the depth-first walk, o_in in a loop
global o_bp uint 1048577
global o_bl uint 1048577
global o_rn uint 1048577
global o_ro uint 1048578
global o_id uint 1048577
global o_pc uint 1048577
global o_p0 uint 1048577
global o_pl uint 2097154
global o_lm uint 1048577
global o_sk uchar 1048577
global o_in uchar 1048577
global o_st uint 1048577
global o_po uint 1048577
global o_hd uint 1048577
global o_hz ulong 1048577
note o_n: 0 blocks of the function, 1 loop stamp, 2 headers, 3 hoisted, 4 merged, 5 rotated, 6 preheaders added,
note 7 loops, 8 in-loop ops before, 9 after, 10 blocks reached, 11 current function, 12 output error (27),
note 13 checks deleted
global o_n ulong 16
text o_msg "opt fns= loops= inloop=-> bce= hoisted= merged= rotated= preheaders=\n"
global o_dig uchar 24
note ---- control flow ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
note successors of block b: br has one (slot 0), cbr two (slots 2, 3), other terminators none
fn op_nsu b uint to ulong
t = get i_bot b
if eq t 0
ret 0
end
op = get i_oop t
if eq op 60
ret 1
end
if eq op 61
ret 2
end
ret 0
end
fn op_su b uint k ulong to uint
t = get i_bot b
if eq get i_oop t 60
ret ir_arg t 0
end
ret ir_arg t uint add k 2
end
note blocks of f in order (o_bl, o_bp), analysis fields cleared
fn op_scan f uint to void
b = get i_fb1 f
k = uint 0
while ne b 0 bound 1048577
put o_bl k b
put o_bp b k
put o_rn b 0
put o_id b 0
put o_pc b 0
put o_lm b 0
k = add k 1
b = get i_bnx b
end
put o_n 0 ulong k
end
note predecessor lists: counts, then starts, then the lists (o_pc ends as the counts again)
fn op_preds to void
n = get o_n 0
for j ulong n bound 1048577
b = get o_bl j
for k ulong op_nsu b bound 2
s = op_su b k
put o_pc s add get o_pc s 1
end
end
c = uint 0
for j ulong n bound 1048577
b = get o_bl j
put o_p0 b c
c = add c get o_pc b
put o_pc b 0
end
for j ulong n bound 1048577
op_pfill get o_bl j
end
end
fn op_pfill b uint to void
for k ulong op_nsu b bound 2
s = op_su b k
put o_pl add get o_p0 s get o_pc s b
put o_pc s add get o_pc s 1
end
end
fn op_pred b uint k ulong to uint
ret get o_pl add ulong get o_p0 b k
end
note reverse postorder from the entry block: an explicit depth-first walk (o_st), postorder into o_po
fn op_rpo to void
e = get o_bl 0
put o_st 0 e
put o_sk e 0
put o_rn e 1
sp = ulong 1
po = ulong 0
while gt sp 0 bound 4194304
b = get o_st sub sp 1
k = ulong get o_sk b
if lt k op_nsu b
put o_sk b uchar add k 1
sp = op_push b k sp
else
sp = sub sp 1
put o_po po b
po = add po 1
end
end
for i ulong po bound 1048577
b = get o_po i
r = sub po i
put o_rn b uint r
put o_ro r b
end
put o_n 10 po
end
fn op_push b uint k ulong sp ulong to ulong
s = op_su b k
if ne get o_rn s 0
ret sp
end
put o_rn s 1
put o_sk s 0
put o_st sp s
ret add sp 1
end
note immediate dominators (Cooper, Harvey and Kennedy: iterate in reverse postorder to a fixed point)
fn op_dom to void
m = get o_n 10
e = get o_ro 1
put o_id e e
ch = true
while ch bound 1048577
ch = false
for r ulong sub m 1 bound 1048577
b = get o_ro add r 2
d = op_idm b
if ne d get o_id b
put o_id b d
ch = true
end
end
end
end
fn op_idm b uint to uint
d = uint 0
for k ulong ulong get o_pc b bound 1048577
p = op_pred b k
if ne get o_id p 0
if eq d 0
d = p
else
d = op_int p d
end
end
end
ret d
end
fn op_int a uint b uint to uint
x = a
y = b
while ne x y bound 1048577
while gt get o_rn x get o_rn y bound 1048577
x = get o_id x
end
while gt get o_rn y get o_rn x bound 1048577
y = get o_id y
end
end
ret x
end
note block a dominates block b
fn op_doms a uint b uint to bool
x = b
while true bound 1048577
if eq x a
ret true
end
y = get o_id x
if eq y x
ret false
end
x = y
end
ret false
end
fn op_ana f uint to void
put o_n 11 ulong f
op_scan f
op_preds
op_rpo
op_dom
end
note ---- loops ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note loop headers of the analysed function into o_hd (count o_n 2): blocks with a predecessor they dominate
fn op_hdrs to void
c = ulong 0
for r ulong get o_n 10 bound 1048577
h = get o_ro add r 1
if op_ishd h
put o_hd c h
c = add c 1
end
end
put o_n 2 c
end
fn op_ishd h uint to bool
for k ulong ulong get o_pc h bound 1048577
if op_doms h op_pred h k
ret true
end
end
ret false
end
note mark the loop of header h with a new stamp (o_lm = o_n 1): h, its latches, and every block that reaches a
note latch without passing h; returns the number of blocks
fn op_mark h uint to ulong
s = uint add get o_n 1 1
put o_n 1 ulong s
put o_lm h s
z = ulong 1
sp = ulong 0
for k ulong ulong get o_pc h bound 1048577
p = op_pred h k
if op_doms h p
if ne get o_lm p s
put o_lm p s
put o_st sp p
sp = add sp 1
z = add z 1
end
end
end
while gt sp 0 bound 1048577
sp = sub sp 1
x = get o_st sp
for k ulong ulong get o_pc x bound 1048577
y = op_pred x k
if ne get o_lm y s
put o_lm y s
put o_st sp y
sp = add sp 1
z = add z 1
end
end
end
ret z
end
fn op_inl b uint to bool
ret eq ulong get o_lm b get o_n 1
end
note the outside predecessor of the marked loop of h that ends in `br h` when it is the only outside one, else 0
fn op_ph h uint to uint
p = uint 0
c = ulong 0
for k ulong ulong get o_pc h bound 1048577
q = op_pred h k
if not op_inl q
p = q
c = add c 1
end
end
if ne c 1
ret 0
end
if ne get i_oop get i_bot p 60
ret 0
end
ret p
end
note ---- lists -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note the op before o in block b (0 when o is first)
fn op_oprv b uint o uint to uint
p = uint 0
x = get i_bo1 b
while ne x o bound 4194305
p = x
x = get i_onx x
end
ret p
end
note take op o out of block b
fn op_unl b uint o uint to void
p = op_oprv b o
if eq p 0
put i_bo1 b get i_onx o
else
put i_onx p get i_onx o
end
if eq get i_bot b o
put i_bot b p
end
put i_bno b sub get i_bno b 1
put i_onx o 0
end
note put op o into block p right before its terminator
fn op_ins p uint o uint to void
t = get i_bot p
q = op_oprv p t
put i_onx o t
if eq q 0
put i_bo1 p o
else
put i_onx q o
end
put i_ob o p
put i_bno p add get i_bno p 1
end
note the block before b in function f (0 when b is first)
fn op_bprv f uint b uint to uint
p = uint 0
x = get i_fb1 f
while ne x b bound 1048577
p = x
x = get i_bnx x
end
ret p
end
note move block b of f to right after block a
fn op_bmv f uint b uint a uint to void
p = op_bprv f b
if eq p 0
put i_fb1 f get i_bnx b
else
put i_bnx p get i_bnx b
end
if eq get i_fbt f b
put i_fbt f p
end
put i_bnx b get i_bnx a
put i_bnx a b
if eq get i_fbt f a
put i_fbt f b
end
end
note every value operand of every op of f that names a takes b instead
fn op_repl f uint a uint b uint to void
x = get i_fb1 f
while ne x 0 bound 1048577
o = get i_bo1 x
while ne o 0 bound 4194305
op_rep1 o a b
o = get i_onx o
end
x = get i_bnx x
end
end
fn op_rep1 o uint a uint b uint to void
op = uint get i_oop o
for k ulong ulong get i_ona o bound 1024
if eq ir_okd op k 0
if eq ir_arg o uint k a
ir_set o uint k b
end
end
end
end
note ---- 1. preheaders ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note add one missing preheader to f; true when one was added (the analysis is then stale)
fn op_pre f uint to bool
op_ana f
op_hdrs
for i ulong get o_n 2 bound 1048577
h = get o_hd i
x = op_mark h
if eq op_ph h 0
op_newp f h
ret true
end
end
ret false
end
note a new block n with h's parameter types, ending in `br h` with them, before h; the outside predecessors of
note the marked loop of h branch to n instead
fn op_newp f uint h uint to void
n = ir_blk f
v = get i_vnx get i_bp1 h
while ne v 0 bound 65
w = ir_bpar n get i_vty v
v = get i_vnx v
end
o = ir_op n 60 0 0 add get i_bnp h 1
ir_set o 0 h
k = uint 1
v = get i_bp1 n
while ne v 0 bound 65
ir_set o k v
k = add k 1
v = get i_vnx v
end
for j ulong ulong get o_pc h bound 1048577
q = op_pred h j
if not op_inl q
op_redir q h n
end
end
op_bmv f n op_bprv f h
put o_n 6 add get o_n 6 1
end
note the terminator of block q branches to n where it branched to h
fn op_redir q uint h uint n uint to void
t = get i_bot q
if eq get i_oop t 60
if eq ir_arg t 0 h
ir_set t 0 n
end
ret
end
for k ulong 2
s = uint add k 2
if eq ir_arg t s h
ir_set t s n
end
end
end
note ---- 2. LICM ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn op_licm f uint to void
op_ana f
op_hdrs
c = get o_n 2
for i ulong c bound 1048577
put o_hz i op_mark get o_hd i
end
op_sort c
for i ulong c bound 1048577
h = get o_hd i
x = op_mark h
p = op_ph h
if ne p 0
op_lic1 p
end
end
end
note headers by loop size, smallest (innermost) first: insertion sort of o_hd by o_hz
fn op_sort c ulong to void
for i ulong c bound 1048577
j = i
while gt j 0 bound 1048577
if le get o_hz sub j 1 get o_hz j
j = 0
else
op_swap sub j 1 j
j = sub j 1
end
end
end
end
fn op_swap a ulong b ulong to void
h = get o_hd a
z = get o_hz a
put o_hd a get o_hd b
put o_hz a get o_hz b
put o_hd b h
put o_hz b z
end
note the marked loop's blocks in reverse postorder, each op that may move to preheader p
fn op_lic1 p uint to void
for r ulong get o_n 10 bound 1048577
b = get o_ro add r 1
if op_inl b
op_licb b p
end
end
end
fn op_licb b uint p uint to void
o = get i_bo1 b
while ne o 0 bound 4194305
nx = get i_onx o
if op_canh o
if op_inv o
op_hoist o b p
end
end
o = nx
end
end
note op o may leave a loop: class P, defines a value, not `shared`
fn op_canh o uint to bool
op = uint get i_oop o
if ne get i_rtk op 0
ret false
end
if eq get i_ors o 0
ret false
end
ret ne op 41
end
note every operand of o past its token slot is defined outside the marked loop
fn op_inv o uint to bool
op = uint get i_oop o
h = ulong ir_htok op
for k ulong ulong get i_ona o bound 1024
if and ge k h eq ir_okd op k 0
if op_inl op_vdb ir_arg o uint k
ret false
end
end
end
ret true
end
note the block that defines value v (0 for the entry token and function parameters)
fn op_vdb v uint to uint
k = get i_vk v
if le k 1
ret 0
end
if eq k 2
ret get i_vo v
end
ret get i_ob get i_vo v
end
note move op o from loop block b to preheader p, or drop it when p already computes the same value
fn op_hoist o uint b uint p uint to void
put o_n 3 add get o_n 3 1
op_unl b o
q = op_same p o
if eq q 0
op_ins p o
ret
end
put o_n 4 add get o_n 4 1
op_repl uint get o_n 11 ir_res o ir_res q
end
note an op of p before its terminator equal to o (same op, type, imm and operands, defines a value), else 0
fn op_same p uint o uint to uint
t = get i_bot p
q = get i_bo1 p
while ne q t bound 4194305
if op_eq q o
ret q
end
q = get i_onx q
end
ret 0
end
fn op_eq q uint o uint to bool
if ne get i_oop q get i_oop o
ret false
end
if ne get i_oty q get i_oty o
ret false
end
if ne get i_oim q get i_oim o
ret false
end
if ne get i_ona q get i_ona o
ret false
end
if eq get i_ors q 0
ret false
end
for k ulong ulong get i_ona o bound 1024
if ne ir_arg q uint k ir_arg o uint k
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note ---- 2. BCE ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn op_bce f uint to void
op_ana f
for j ulong get o_n 0 bound 1048577
b = get o_bl j
if ne get o_rn b 0
op_bceb b
end
end
end
fn op_bceb b uint to void
o = get i_bo1 b
while ne o 0 bound 4194305
nx = get i_onx o
op = get i_oop o
if eq op 79
if op_inb o b
op_drop b o true
end
end
if eq op 74
if ne op_cv ir_arg o 1 0
op_drop b o false
end
end
o = nx
end
end
note value v is defined by a `const`
fn op_isc v uint to bool
if ne get i_vk v 4
ret false
end
ret eq get i_oop get i_vo v 1
end
note the bits of const v, 0 when v is not a const
fn op_cv v uint to ulong
if not op_isc v
ret 0
end
ret get i_oim get i_vo v
end
note element count of the ARRAY that REF value r refers to, 0 when r is not a REF to an ARRAY
fn op_alen r uint to ulong
t = get i_vty r
if lt t 32
ret 0
end
if ne get i_tk t 4
ret 0
end
a = get i_t1 t
if lt a 32
ret 0
end
if ne get i_tk a 2
ret 0
end
ret ulong get i_t2 a
end
note chk.bounds o (tok, r, i, e) in block b cannot fail
fn op_inb o uint b uint to bool
e = op_cv ir_arg o 3
if eq e 0
ret false
end
l = op_alen ir_arg o 1
if lt l e
ret false
end
x = op_ub ir_arg o 2 b
if eq x 0
ret false
end
ret le x add sub l e 1
end
note the least X with v < X known in block b from a const or the tests on b's dominator path; 0 none
fn op_ub v uint b uint to ulong
if op_isc v
c = op_cv v
if eq c 18446744073709551615
ret 0
end
ret add c 1
end
x = ulong 0
d = b
while true bound 1048577
y = op_edge v d
if ne y 0
if or eq x 0 lt y x
x = y
end
end
p = get o_id d
if eq p d
ret x
end
d = p
end
ret x
end
note the bound X with v < X that block d's one incoming edge proves, else 0: d has one predecessor, it
note ends in `cbr` with d as exactly one target, and the condition compares v with a const
fn op_edge v uint d uint to ulong
if ne get o_pc d 1
ret 0
end
t = get i_bot op_pred d 0
if ne get i_oop t 61
ret 0
end
if eq ir_arg t 2 ir_arg t 3
ret 0
end
c = ir_arg t 1
if ne get i_vk c 4
ret 0
end
q = get i_vo c
op = ulong get i_oop q
if or lt op 32 gt op 35
ret 0
end
if eq ir_arg t 2 d
ret op_cmpx q op 0 v
end
ret op_cmpx q op 1 v
end
note compare q `a OP b` (32 lt, 33 le, 34 gt, 35 ge) seen true (n 0) or false (n 1, the negation 67 - OP):
note the X with v < X when the relation bounds v above by a const; 0 otherwise
fn op_cmpx q uint op ulong n ulong v uint to ulong
k = op
if eq n 1
k = sub 67 op
end
s = ir_arg q 0
w = ir_arg q 1
if ge k 34
s = ir_arg q 1
w = ir_arg q 0
end
if ne s v
ret 0
end
if not op_isc w
ret 0
end
c = op_cv w
if or eq k 32 eq k 34
ret c
end
if eq c 18446744073709551615
ret 0
end
ret add c 1
end
note delete check o of block b: uses of its output token take its input token; with fk, a
note `fact.inbounds 1` on its (r, i, e) takes its place
fn op_drop b uint o uint fk bool to void
if fk
x = ir_op b 92 0 1 3
op_unl b x
op_insb b x o
ir_set x 0 ir_arg o 1
ir_set x 1 ir_arg o 2
ir_set x 2 ir_arg o 3
end
op_repl uint get o_n 11 ir_otok o ir_arg o 0
op_unl b o
put o_n 13 add get o_n 13 1
end
note put op x into block b right before op o
fn op_insb b uint x uint o uint to void
q = op_oprv b o
put i_onx x o
if eq q 0
put i_bo1 b x
else
put i_onx q x
end
put i_ob x b
put i_bno b add get i_bno b 1
end
note ---- 4. ROT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn op_rot f uint to void
op_ana f
op_hdrs
for i ulong get o_n 2 bound 1048577
h = get o_hd i
x = op_mark h
op_rot1 f h
end
end
fn op_rot1 f uint h uint to void
t = get i_bot h
if ne get i_oop t 61
ret
end
if eq op_inl ir_arg t 2 op_inl ir_arg t 3
ret
end
u = op_latch h
if or eq u 0 eq u h
ret
end
if ne get i_oop get i_bot u 60
ret
end
if eq get i_bnx u h
ret
end
op_bmv f h u
put o_n 5 add get o_n 5 1
end
note the one predecessor of h inside its marked loop, else 0
fn op_latch h uint to uint
u = uint 0
c = ulong 0
for k ulong ulong get o_pc h bound 1048577
q = op_pred h k
if op_inl q
u = q
c = add c 1
end
end
if ne c 1
ret 0
end
ret u
end
note ---- driver and counts ------------------------------------------------------------------------
note ops in the blocks of f that lie in a loop; adds f's loops to o_n 7 when k is 0
fn op_cnt f uint k ulong to ulong
op_ana f
op_hdrs
for j ulong get o_n 0 bound 1048577
put o_in get o_bl j 0
end
for i ulong get o_n 2 bound 1048577
x = op_mark get o_hd i
op_inmk
end
if eq k 0
put o_n 7 add get o_n 7 get o_n 2
end
c = ulong 0
for j ulong get o_n 0 bound 1048577
b = get o_bl j
if ne get o_in b 0
c = add c op_nex b
end
end
ret c
end
note executing ops of block b (facts 90..93 do not run)
fn op_nex b uint to ulong
c = ulong 0
o = get i_bo1 b
while ne o 0 bound 4194305
op = get i_oop o
if or lt op 90 gt op 93
c = add c 1
end
o = get i_onx o
end
ret c
end
fn op_inmk to void
for j ulong get o_n 0 bound 1048577
b = get o_bl j
if op_inl b
put o_in b 1
end
end
end
note optimize every function of the unit read into the ir.om tables
fn op_run to void
for j ulong 16
put o_n j 0
end
for i ulong get i_n 3 bound 65536
op_fn uint add i 1
end
end
fn op_fn f uint to void
if lt get i_fnb f 2
ret
end
put o_n 8 add get o_n 8 op_cnt f 0
go = true
while go bound 65536
go = op_pre f
end
op_bce f
op_licm f
op_rot f
put o_n 9 add get o_n 9 op_cnt f 1
end
note the opt-count line on stdout; 27 when it cannot be written
fn op_put to int
op_say 0 8
op_num get i_n 3
op_say 8 15
op_num get o_n 7
op_say 15 23
op_num get o_n 8
op_say 23 25
op_num get o_n 9
op_say 25 30
op_num get o_n 13
op_say 30 39
op_num get o_n 3
op_say 39 47
op_num get o_n 4
op_say 47 56
op_num get o_n 5
op_say 56 68
op_num get o_n 6
op_say 68 69
ret int get o_n 12
end
fn op_say a ulong b ulong to void
k = write 1 o_msg a sub b a
if ne k long sub b a
put o_n 12 27
end
end
fn op_num v ulong to void
x = v
i = ulong 24
for j ulong 21
i = sub i 1
put o_dig i uchar add 48 rem x 10
x = div x 10
if eq x 0
k = write 1 o_dig i sub 24 i
if ne k long sub 24 i
put o_n 12 27
end
ret
end
end
end
